;; The world seat: plays the outside world an org's brief implies, one
;; simulated day per firing, for seven days. It only ever sits on a
;; clone (docs/spec-demo-clones.md): its rows are the week the film
;; shows before the person merges the org. Epic cafa6106, M3c.
{:template
 {:params {:brief "The org_plan's brief, the one paragraph the person typed: what this business is and does."
           :kind "The org's kind whose create door the outside world knocks on (the request a customer files), by its name."
           :cast "The cast members the world plays, as the seed's :cast names them, comma-separated: the customers, suppliers and callers whose words the rows carry. Never the org's own people."
           :day_one "The date day 1 is, as the clone's seed resolves [:days 0] (YYYY-MM-DD). Day k is day_one plus k-1 days."
           :domain_id "The id of the org's domain row: the seat's :domain ref."}
  :note "Seat this only in a clone's seed, never in an org that is live: it writes rows a real customer did not file. Seven firings make the week; an eighth finds day 7 already written and does nothing."}
 :seat
 {:name "world"
  :mode "fired"
  :rows_per_firing 1
  :cadence_seconds 3600
  :fire_interval_seconds 300
  :max_open_sittings 1
  :standing_ttl_seconds 604800
  :budget_usd_per_week 5M
  :sitting_budget_tokens 80000
  :sitting_idle_seconds 1800
  :keep_transcripts "fired"
  :transcript_days 30
  :acts_as_cast true
  :domain "{{domain_id}}"
  :charter "You play the outside world for one business across seven simulated days. The business is this: {{brief}} From that brief, imagine the customers, suppliers and events a business like this meets in its first week, including the hard ones: a late payer, a double booking, a complaint, a cancellation, a request too thin to act on. Each firing is one day. Find the day: read the {{kind}} rows you already created; the next day is one past the latest day they carry, starting at day 1 on {{day_one}}; day k is {{day_one}} plus k-1 days. After day 7, do nothing. For the day, create the two to four {{kind}} rows a real day would bring, through its own create door, each in the words of one cast member ({{cast}}) and naming that member in the row, with every date in it on or after day k's date. Across the week, file at least one the org's guards will refuse. A refusal is part of the week the film shows, not an error: never retry it to make it pass, never change a row after you create it, and never take a door the org's own seats hold; they answer."
  :instructions "You sit in `world`. For your one day: list the {{kind}} rows you created (waymark_query kind \"{{kind}}\", return \"summary\") to find the day. Then create that day's rows with waymark_invoke kind \"{{kind}}\", action \"create\", no id. When a create refuses, leave it: that refusal is the day's event. When halted or parked, say why and stop. When the Stop hook asks you to close the sitting, make that one call; the note names the day and each row you created or that refused."
  :scope [{:kind "{{kind}}" :actions ["create"]}]
  :delivers [{:kind "{{kind}}" :action "create"}]}}
